::: {.doc-subject}

Get attribute values for nodes.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L7441-L7533){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
Graph.get_node_attrs(node_attr, nodes=None)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Extracts a specific attribute from one or more nodes. Only returns entries for nodes that
have the specified attribute set. Useful for collecting properties across the graph.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[node_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   Attribute name to extract.

<code>[nodes]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[int | str] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Optional list of node IDs (int) or labels (str) to query. If `None`, queries all nodes.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [dict[int, any]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   Dictionary mapping node IDs to attribute values. Only includes nodes that have the
    attribute set.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

Get specific attribute from all nodes:

::: {#54b887fc .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import edgecase as ec

graph = (
    ec.Graph()
    .add_node(label="A", type="user", score=95)
    .add_node(label="B", type="admin", score=88)
    .add_node(label="C", type="user", score=92)
)

scores = graph.get_node_attrs("score")

# Returns dict with node IDs as keys: {1: 95, 2: 88, 3: 92}
scores
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```
{2: 88, 3: 92, 1: 95}
```
:::
:::


::: {#52e73abf .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
types = graph.get_node_attrs("type")

# Returns: {1: 'user', 2: 'admin', 3: 'user'}
types
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```
{2: 'admin', 3: 'user', 1: 'user'}
```
:::
:::


Get attribute from specific nodes using node IDs:

::: {#98efbf53 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
graph = (
    ec.Graph()
    .add_node(label="A", type="user", score=95)
    .add_node(label="B", type="admin", score=88)
    .add_node(label="C", type="user", score=92)
)
node_ids = list(graph.get_node_ids())
user_scores = graph.get_node_attrs("score", nodes=[node_ids[0], node_ids[2]])

# Returns {1: 95, 3: 92}
user_scores
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}
```
{2: 88, 1: 95}
```
:::
:::


Can also use labels:

::: {#8b725632 .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
graph = (
    ec.Graph()
    .add_node(label="A", type="user", score=95)
    .add_node(label="B", type="admin", score=88)
    .add_node(label="C", type="user", score=92)
)
user_scores = graph.get_node_attrs("score", nodes=["A", "C"])
user_scores
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}
```
{1: 95, 3: 92}
```
:::
:::
